## [:< ##

# name  = plugin.host-edit.actions.tab_info
# descr = host-actions plugin's self-description
# param = -none-

## the 'host actions' tab : drive the add-host FLOW [ host-edit.flow.* ] from
## inside the form, on EVERY host record -- connect .. pin .. certify without
## leaving the frame.  this is host-edit's mirror of
## plugin.user-edit.key-actions.tab_info's own role : the same pinned
## SYNTHESISED field, Enter opening an in-frame editor.control.prompt [ masked
## for the owner-key passphrase ], nothing leaving the event loop.
##
## pinned_keys => ['host_actions'], exactly like key-actions' own choice :
## form.handler.stdin_key's Right-entry trigger requires BOTH plugin => ...
## on the field def AND the field's name present in the registry's by_key map,
## and the synthesised 'host_actions' field is pushed by the record source's
## synth_fields builder [ plugin.host-edit.actions.build_field, reached
## through form.schema_from_record's generic hook ], never present in a real
## record's fields -- no collision : 'host_actions' appears nowhere in
## host-edit.record.default_fields.
##
## q|..|, NOT qw|..| : qw splits on WHITESPACE, so qw| host actions | would
## collapse into label => 'host' plus a stray 'actions' key -- the same trap
## plugin.user-edit.key-actions.tab_info's own header documents
return {
    qw| label |       => q| host actions |,
    qw| pinned_keys | => [qw| host_actions |],
};

